          "answer": "The symptoms you described, including facial asymmetry and speech difficulty, involve the neurological system.\n\nWhen these types of symptoms appear suddenly and then resolve, clinicians consider several possibilities for a transient neurological event. One important consideration is a transient ischemic attack (TIA), sometimes called a \"mini-stroke,\" which involves a temporary disruption of blood flow to part of the brain. Another possibility could be a migraine with aura, which can cause temporary neurological symptoms.\n\nIt is important to discuss these symptoms with a clinician to understand their cause and to rule out serious conditions, especially since symptoms like these can sometimes be a warning sign.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
